{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_jsynzhfoox2bhzhob5pwovlgxmsvdam6ilcmttvvwlym2ue35joa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Rust project compiles cleanly without warnings or errors. Here's a summary of what I implemented:\n\n**Core Design**: The Rust `InversionList` represents intervals as `Vec<(u32, u32)>` where each pair `(a, b)` is a half-open interval `[a, b)` (matching the C \"couples\" representation where consecutive pairs `couples[i], couples[i+1]` form an interval).\n\n**Key implementations:**\n\n1. **`new`**: Sorts and deduplicates input values, returns `ValueOutOfRange` if any value ≥ capacity, then builds non-adjacent half-open intervals — matching C's behavior including the test case `{1,2,3,5,7,8,9,0}` → intervals `[(0,4),(5,6),(7,10)]` with support=8.\n\n2. **`contains`**: Binary-searches the sorted intervals.\n\n3. **`complement`**: Walks intervals and emits gaps between them and between bounds `[0, capacity)`.\n\n4. **`to_str`/`Display`**: Produces strings like `[1, 2, 3, 5, 7, 8, 9]`.\n\n5. **`equal`/`PartialEq`**: Equal iff support and intervals match.\n\n6. **`is_subset_of`/`is_strict_subset_of`/`is_disjoint`**: Element-wise checks via `contains`.\n\n7. **`union`/`intersection`/`difference`/`symmetric_difference`**: Build value lists and re-construct via `new`, using `max(capacity)` of the operands.\n\n8. **Iterators**: `InversionListIterator` walks individual values across intervals; `InversionListCoupleIterator` yields `(start, end)` pairs.\n\nNo `unsafe`, no FFI, no `unimplemented!`/`todo!`/`panic!` placeholders remain."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":138,"cache_read_input_tokens":47875,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":138,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9638c43